		Heading 1:
			Text: Merge borders
		Paragraph: With a `Border` on each cell, the line between two cells is drawn once, centered on it, with the wider border and its color: the line under the header is the 1.5 of the header. With `Merge borders: false` in the `Box` of the `Table`, each cell draws its own border, and two neighbors draw two lines side by side.
